---
source: tests/workflow.rs
expression: cli.checkpoint()
---
$ markoff list
# Tasks
$ markoff add work 'Fix bug'
markoff: no section 'work', there are none yet
[exit 1]
$ markoff add --section work
work
$ markoff add work 'Fix bug'
work/fix-bug
$ markoff add work 'Call Bob'
work/call-bob
$ markoff show work/fix-bgu
markoff: no section or task 'work/fix-bgu', did you mean 'work/fix-bug'?
[exit 1]
$ markoff add wrok Another
markoff: no section 'wrok', did you mean 'work'?
[exit 1]
$ markoff done work
markoff: 'work' is a section, not a task, see 'markoff list work'
[exit 1]
$ markoff edit work --title Job
markoff: 'work' is a section, only --name changes it
[exit 1]
$ markoff move work/call-bob --after work/call-bob
markoff: 'work/call-bob' is the task to move, it cannot go next to itself
[exit 1]
$ markoff delete work/fix-bug work/nope
markoff: no section or task 'work/nope', see 'markoff list'
[exit 1]
$ markoff delete work
markoff: 'work' is not empty, delete or move its tasks first: work/fix-bug, work/call-bob
[exit 1]
$ markoff lsit
error: unrecognized subcommand 'lsit'

  tip: a similar subcommand exists: 'list'

Usage: markoff [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

For more information, try '--help'.
[exit 2]
$ markoff edit work/fix-bug
error: the following required arguments were not provided:
  <--title <TITLE>|--body <TEXT>|--append <TEXT>|--name <NAME>>

Usage: markoff edit <--title <TITLE>|--body <TEXT>|--append <TEXT>|--name <NAME>> <ID>

For more information, try '--help'.
[exit 2]
$ markoff list --from [date]
error: the following required arguments were not provided:
  --archive

Usage: markoff list --archive --from <YYYY-MM-DD> [SECTION]...

For more information, try '--help'.
[exit 2]
$ markoff list
# Tasks

## work
- Fix the bug (work/fix-bug)
- Call Bob (work/call-bob)
$ markoff done work/fix-bug
.archive/[date]/work/fix-the-bug
$ markoff edit .archive/[date]/work/fix-the-bug --append late
markoff: '.archive/[date]/work/fix-the-bug' is archived, archived tasks are read-only
[exit 1]
$ markoff list --archive --filter fix
# Archive from [date] to [date]

## [date]
### work
- Fix the bug (.archive/[date]/work/fix-the-bug)

--- .archive/

--- .archive/[date]/

--- .archive/[date]/work/

--- .archive/[date]/work/fix-the-bug.md
# Fix the bug

--- .markoff
# work
call-bob

--- work/

--- work/call-bob.md
# Call Bob
